==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*čьrnъ}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*kr̥snós||black}}. Cognates include Old Church Slavonic {{term|sc=Cyrs|чрънъ|tr=črŭnŭ||black|lang=cu}}, Bulgarian {{term|черен|lang=bg}}, Serbo-Croatian {{term|црн|lang=sh}}/{{term|crn|lang=sh}}, Slovene {{term|črn|lang=sl}}, Slovak {{term|čierny|lang=sk}}; Norwegian and Swedish {{term|harr||grayling|lang=sv}}, Sanskrit {{term|कृष्ण|sc=Deva|lang=sa}}, Old Prussian {{term|kirsnan||black|lang=prg}}.

